libretro-core.c: WHDLoad, CD and archive exports for host-generated boots

PEEKaboo boots WHDLoad archives and CD images from a .uae it writes itself, so the core's
content-loader paths never run for them. Three additions:

- adm_whdload_prepare() installs the embedded WHDLoad payload exactly as a WHDLoad content
  load does. The WHDLoad.prefs rewrite and the file-mode installation move out of
  retro_create_config() into whdload_prepare_prefs() / whdload_prepare_file_mode(), which
  both paths now call, so there is one implementation.
- adm_cd_insert() / adm_cd_eject() / adm_cd_get_image() change CD0 while the machine runs.
  The disk-control index selects a floppy drive in this build, so a disc cannot go through it.
- adm_extract_archive() exposes zip_uncompress / sevenzip_uncompress, so .7z disc sets can be
  unpacked without the host linking 7-Zip.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

